A full-stack job management application built with Node.js, Express, MongoDB, and JWT authentication using httpOnly cookies.
Users can register, log in, and manage their job applications (create, read, update status, delete).

The frontend is served statically through public/ and communicates with the backend using fetch() with credentials: "include".

🚀 Features

<!-- Authentication -->

Register users with name, email, password

Login using email and password

JWT stored in httpOnly cookies

Protected routes using authenticateUser middleware

Cookies use sameSite: strict for security

<!-- Job Management -->

Create a job (company, position, status)

Retrieve all jobs created by current user

Update job status (pending / interview / decline)

Delete job

All job routes require valid authentication

<!-- Frontend -->

Pure HTML/CSS/JS (no frameworks)

Auth pages for register/login

Main dashboard (main.html) that:

Loads user’s jobs

Creates jobs

Updates job status

Deletes jobs

Handles 401/403 authentication errors

Cookie-based authentication (automatic if logged in)

